E.g. pacify and taming music probably sound very similar, so you could
just use one song that causes different effects depending on various
circumstances. Same for berserk/haste...
Basically you seem to have:

peaceful music (sleep/pacify/taming)
military music (berserk/haste pets)
scary music

Some circumstances that can make a difference for the effect of a song:
  - the instrument
  - skilled bards produce more powerful effects
  - wounded monster won't listen that much to peaceful music
  - if the bard is unseen a scary/confusing effect works better
  - some monsters-types resist (deafness)
  - surely some demons like scary music and hate peaceful music
  - ... more monster-type special cases
  - singing a lot could dry out your throat (instead of using up Power
    you have to drink potions to maintain the ability to sing)

Some thoughts on skill/failure rate
  - having to raise music skill a lot before you can use songs is
    probably annoying, so even low-level low-skill bards should have
    a good chance to produce some useful effect.
  - at skilled level you can play instruments while blind and get
    more powerful effects
  - playing peaceful music while wounded is difficult
  - aggressive songs could be easier to play while wounded

